FILE: /private/tmp/SPEC-RELEASE-CONVERGENCE-002.draft.json
TITLE: 
AC AC-001: {"id":"AC-001","criterion":"Every operation role has one production observer that returns exactly Absent, Exact with safe typed evidence, Conflict with a closed reason, or Unverifiable with an actionable transient diagnostic. Execute, reconcile, pre-effect checks, post-effect checks, and interruption recovery call that same observer rather than reconstructing provider semantics in sibling paths.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-002: {"id":"AC-002","criterion":"Execution observes every operation in canonical DAG order regardless of whether the optional journal says Pending, Attempting, Published, AlreadySatisfied, Failed, or Blocked. Exact is recorded as satisfied without mutation; Absent is mutated at most once in that invocation and must be Exact on post-effect observation; Conflict or Unverifiable exits nonzero without mutating that operation or any dependent operation.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-003: {"id":"AC-003","criterion":"A missing, unreadable, stale, or entirely lost execution-state file cannot widen authority or prevent recovery. A fresh runner given the same immutable intent and artifact manifest observes exact existing objects, skips their mutation, creates only absent objects, and converges to the same result; state remains an atomically persisted diagnostic journal bound to the intent.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-004: {"id":"AC-004","criterion":"Release execute returns exit status zero only after every intended operation is observed Exact in the same final pass and a matching ReleaseReceipt is atomically persisted. Any Pending, Attempting, Failed, Blocked, Absent, Conflict, Unverifiable, missing operation, missing receipt, or receipt-write failure exits nonzero and names the incomplete operation and recovery action.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-005: {"id":"AC-005","criterion":"A receipt records the intent digest, exact operation roster, observation time-independent safe evidence identities and digests, and whether each object was newly produced or already present. It is output evidence only: execute and reconcile re-observe providers on every invocation and never accept receipt bytes as proof that an external object still exists or still matches.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-006: {"id":"AC-006","criterion":"Registry observation compares the provider's immutable published artifact set with the matching expected RegistryPackage entries in the intent-bound artifact manifest: crates.io-compatible publication verifies the .crate checksum, npm verifies the packed tarball integrity or bytes, and PyPI verifies the complete expected distribution-file name and SHA-256 set. A present exact set is prominently reported and never republished; missing is publishable; a partial set, different digest, extra conflicting distribution, or provider response that cannot prove equality is fatal.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-007: {"id":"AC-007","criterion":"Remote tag observation queries the configured remote rather than local refs and proves the exact tag name resolves to the intended source commit and required annotated-tag content. A matching local-only tag is neither Exact nor post-push confirmation; a conflicting remote tag is fatal; after creation or push, the remote is re-observed before any forge-release or asset operation becomes eligible.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-008: {"id":"AC-008","criterion":"GitHub Release observation uses supported GitHub CLI or API arguments, classifies the real nonzero-exit HTTP 404 contract as Absent, preserves 401, 403, 429, 5xx, malformed, and transport results as Unverifiable, and proves release identity through the separately verified remote tag rather than target_commitish. Exactness also covers the required draft/prerelease policy and final asset roster.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-009: {"id":"AC-009","criterion":"GitHub asset observation addresses the exact ProductReleaseId and slot file name, downloads or queries immutable digest-capable data, and proves byte length and SHA-256 against the artifact manifest. An existing same-name asset with a different or unverifiable digest is fatal and is never overwritten; after an upload, the asset is re-observed as Exact before completion.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-010: {"id":"AC-010","criterion":"Release reconcile is structurally read-only and emits a complete report for every operation, not merely a list of locally eligible Pending entries. It requires no ApplyPermit, invokes no registry publish, Git push, GitHub creation, or upload route, and exits nonzero when the intended release is not completely Exact while preserving the full observation report in JSON output.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-011: {"id":"AC-011","criterion":"Boundary tests exercise realistic subprocess contracts: real Git with a bare remote for absent, exact, and conflicting tags; argv parsing compatible with the installed gh CLI; gh HTTP 404 with its real nonzero exit; 401, 403, 429, and 5xx failures; and local HTTP registry fixtures for absent, exact, conflicting, and unverifiable artifact metadata. An argv-insensitive fake or exit-zero 404 alone cannot satisfy this criterion.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-012: {"id":"AC-012","criterion":"An interruption test stops at each boundary between attempt persistence, provider mutation, provider success, post-effect observation, terminal-state persistence, and receipt persistence, then resumes with both the same journal and no journal on a fresh runner. Every case either converges without repeating an Exact effect or exits nonzero for Conflict/Unverifiable; no case can return successful incomplete state.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-013: {"id":"AC-013","criterion":"The graph-private prepared operation remains the only effect and observation input. Provider adapters cannot accept free-form package, version, endpoint, tag, repository, asset name, or digest values from CLI flags, workflow environment, mutable configuration, or execution state after the intent has been validated.","is_error_case":true}
FILE: /private/tmp/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.draft.json
TITLE: 
AC AC-001: {"id":"AC-001","criterion":"The reviewed managed release pull request merge is the sole human approval event. The production workflow contains no environment-policy job, required-reviewer API check, protected Environment reviewer gate, or second manual approval; merge automatically proceeds through plan, build, attest, execute, and final verify when checks pass.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-002: {"id":"AC-002","criterion":"The automatic path proves that the triggering commit is exactly one verified merge of the canonical managed release branch, derives the immutable intent from that merge and its reviewed decision, and rejects direct pushes, unrelated pull requests, ambiguous merges, mutable branch tips, or an intent whose digest/source does not match.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-003: {"id":"AC-003","criterion":"Planning has read-only repository permission and no release credentials. Build jobs have only source-read plus attestation/OIDC permissions. The execute job alone receives registry credentials and contents-write permission, only after it independently validates the intent, source commit, complete artifact manifest, bytes, checksums, and attestations. Removing the Environment gate does not widen any earlier job's permissions.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-004: {"id":"AC-004","criterion":"The build stage derives its matrix from the immutable intent and produces exactly the aarch64-apple-darwin, x86_64-unknown-linux-musl, aarch64-unknown-linux-musl, and wasm32-wasip1 payloads plus all registry-package artifacts. A fan-in job validates the complete slot roster, creates deterministic archives and SHA256SUMS, records the artifact manifest, and ensures each required file has a GitHub attestation before execution can start.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-005: {"id":"AC-005","criterion":"Intent, artifact manifest, payload, checksum, and receipt handoffs are downloaded outside the trusted source checkout and are retained and addressable for at least 30 days. Retention improves recoverability but grants no authority: every downloaded byte and identifier is revalidated against the immutable intent and source commit.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-006: {"id":"AC-006","criterion":"A workflow_dispatch recovery can name an exact historical full release commit and either rebuild its intent-bound artifacts or consume a named prior run whose intent digest is supplied. It verifies the original managed-PR merge, plan digest, source commit, and artifact bindings, then uses external-state convergence; it never substitutes current main, latest, a different run's artifacts, or runner-local state.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-007: {"id":"AC-007","criterion":"The execute job invokes the core CLI once with the exact intent, artifact manifest, artifact directory, state path, and receipt path. Workflow shell does not publish registries, derive tag names, create releases, upload product assets, classify already-present responses, or decide completion independently of the CLI.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-008: {"id":"AC-008","criterion":"The release workflow fails unless the CLI emits and the workflow validates a complete receipt for the same intent digest. The receipt and complete observation report are uploaded even on failure when safely available; a green execute or workflow conclusion without a valid complete receipt is impossible.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-009: {"id":"AC-009","criterion":"The isolated rehearsal uses a dedicated non-production GitHub repository or equivalent isolated forge namespace plus non-production Cargo, npm, and PyPI registry endpoints and credentials. Endpoint allowlists fail closed so rehearsal can never address production registries, the production repository, or a production callisto@X.Y.Z tag.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-010: {"id":"AC-010","criterion":"One rehearsal covers managed release-PR merge, immutable plan, every registry artifact build, all four product builds and native/WASM smoke tests, checksums, GitHub attestations, product tag, draft release, asset uploads, final release publication, final observation, and receipt without using production publication credentials.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-011: {"id":"AC-011","criterion":"Rehearsal failpoints can stop after each provider mutation and before each following journal or receipt write. Each failpoint is resumed in a fresh job or run without its predecessor's RUNNER_TEMP state, and the second run must converge without duplicate mutation or false success. Conflict, unverifiable, expired-handoff, and wrong-source negative cases must also fail with actionable diagnostics.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-012: {"id":"AC-012","criterion":"The production release boundary cannot be changed or used for the first production release until the current release implementation and workflow pass the full rehearsal suite. Subsequent changes to release intent schemas, provider adapters, operation DAG, build matrix, attestation policy, or workflow handoff contract require the rehearsal gate again.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-013: {"id":"AC-013","criterion":"Superseded pre-v1 release routes and documentation are removed in the same change: there is one supported release plan/inspect/reconcile/execute family, one release-PR action, and one product-release workflow. No command is retained merely as a legacy preview, and no documentation describes the old per-package, Environment-gated, journal-authoritative, or shell-owned release path.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-014: {"id":"AC-014","criterion":"All third-party Actions remain pinned to immutable commit SHAs; concurrency prevents two executions for the same ProductReleaseId; logs and uploaded diagnostics contain no credentials; and every shell interpolation crossing from workflow inputs is passed through a named environment variable and validated before use.","is_error_case":true}
