AC AC-009: {"id":"AC-009","criterion":"GitHub asset observation addresses the exact ProductReleaseId and slot file name, downloads or queries immutable digest-capable data, and proves byte length and SHA-256 against the artifact manifest. An existing same-name asset with a different or unverifiable digest is fatal and is never overwritten; after an upload, the asset is re-observed as Exact before completion.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-010: {"id":"AC-010","criterion":"Release reconcile is structurally read-only and emits a complete report for every operation, not merely a list of locally eligible Pending entries. It requires no ApplyPermit, invokes no registry publish, Git push, GitHub creation, or upload route, and exits nonzero when the intended release is not completely Exact while preserving the full observation report in JSON output.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-011: {"id":"AC-011","criterion":"Boundary tests exercise realistic subprocess contracts: real Git with a bare remote for absent, exact, and conflicting tags; argv parsing compatible with the installed gh CLI; gh HTTP 404 with its real nonzero exit; 401, 403, 429, and 5xx failures; and local HTTP registry fixtures for absent, exact, conflicting, and unverifiable artifact metadata. An argv-insensitive fake or exit-zero 404 alone cannot satisfy this criterion.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-012: {"id":"AC-012","criterion":"An interruption test stops at each boundary between attempt persistence, provider mutation, provider success, post-effect observation, terminal-state persistence, and receipt persistence, then resumes with both the same journal and no journal on a fresh runner. Every case either converges without repeating an Exact effect or exits nonzero for Conflict/Unverifiable; no case can return successful incomplete state.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-013: {"id":"AC-013","criterion":"The graph-private prepared operation remains the only effect and observation input. Provider adapters cannot accept free-form package, version, endpoint, tag, repository, asset name, or digest values from CLI flags, workflow environment, mutable configuration, or execution state after the intent has been validated.","is_error_case":true}
FILE: /private/tmp/SPEC-RELEASE-ORCHESTRATION-003.draft.json
TITLE: 
AC AC-001: {"id":"AC-001","criterion":"The reviewed managed release pull request merge is the sole human approval event. The production workflow contains no environment-policy job, required-reviewer API check, protected Environment reviewer gate, or second manual approval; merge automatically proceeds through plan, build, attest, execute, and final verify when checks pass.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-002: {"id":"AC-002","criterion":"The automatic path proves that the triggering commit is exactly one verified merge of the canonical managed release branch, derives the immutable intent from that merge and its reviewed decision, and rejects direct pushes, unrelated pull requests, ambiguous merges, mutable branch tips, or an intent whose digest/source does not match.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-003: {"id":"AC-003","criterion":"Planning has read-only repository permission and no release credentials. Build jobs have only source-read plus attestation/OIDC permissions. The execute job alone receives registry credentials and contents-write permission, only after it independently validates the intent, source commit, complete artifact manifest, bytes, checksums, and attestations. Removing the Environment gate does not widen any earlier job's permissions.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-004: {"id":"AC-004","criterion":"The build stage derives its matrix from the immutable intent and produces exactly the aarch64-apple-darwin, x86_64-unknown-linux-musl, aarch64-unknown-linux-musl, and wasm32-wasip1 payloads plus all registry-package artifacts. A fan-in job validates the complete slot roster, creates deterministic archives and SHA256SUMS, records the artifact manifest, and ensures each required file has a GitHub attestation before execution can start.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-005: {"id":"AC-005","criterion":"Intent, artifact manifest, payload, checksum, and receipt handoffs are downloaded outside the trusted source checkout and are retained and addressable for at least 30 days. Retention improves recoverability but grants no authority: every downloaded byte and identifier is revalidated against the immutable intent and source commit.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-006: {"id":"AC-006","criterion":"A workflow_dispatch recovery can name an exact historical full release commit and either rebuild its intent-bound artifacts or consume a named prior run whose intent digest is supplied. It verifies the original managed-PR merge, plan digest, source commit, and artifact bindings, then uses external-state convergence; it never substitutes current main, latest, a different run's artifacts, or runner-local state.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-007: {"id":"AC-007","criterion":"The execute job invokes the core CLI once with the exact intent, artifact manifest, artifact directory, state path, and receipt path. Workflow shell does not publish registries, derive tag names, create releases, upload product assets, classify already-present responses, or decide completion independently of the CLI.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-008: {"id":"AC-008","criterion":"The release workflow fails unless the CLI emits and the workflow validates a complete receipt for the same intent digest. The receipt and complete observation report are uploaded even on failure when safely available; a green execute or workflow conclusion without a valid complete receipt is impossible.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-009: {"id":"AC-009","criterion":"The isolated rehearsal uses a dedicated non-production GitHub repository or equivalent isolated forge namespace plus non-production Cargo, npm, and PyPI registry endpoints and credentials. Endpoint allowlists fail closed so rehearsal can never address production registries, the production repository, or a production callisto@X.Y.Z tag.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-010: {"id":"AC-010","criterion":"One rehearsal covers managed release-PR merge, immutable plan, every registry artifact build, all four product builds and native/WASM smoke tests, checksums, GitHub attestations, product tag, draft release, asset uploads, final release publication, final observation, and receipt without using production publication credentials.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-011: {"id":"AC-011","criterion":"Rehearsal failpoints can stop after each provider mutation and before each following journal or receipt write. Each failpoint is resumed in a fresh job or run without its predecessor's RUNNER_TEMP state, and the second run must converge without duplicate mutation or false success. Conflict, unverifiable, expired-handoff, and wrong-source negative cases must also fail with actionable diagnostics.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-012: {"id":"AC-012","criterion":"The production release boundary cannot be changed or used for the first production release until the current release implementation and workflow pass the full rehearsal suite. Subsequent changes to release intent schemas, provider adapters, operation DAG, build matrix, attestation policy, or workflow handoff contract require the rehearsal gate again.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-013: {"id":"AC-013","criterion":"Superseded pre-v1 release routes and documentation are removed in the same change: there is one supported release plan/inspect/reconcile/execute family, one release-PR action, and one product-release workflow. No command is retained merely as a legacy preview, and no documentation describes the old per-package, Environment-gated, journal-authoritative, or shell-owned release path.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-014: {"id":"AC-014","criterion":"All third-party Actions remain pinned to immutable commit SHAs; concurrency prevents two executions for the same ProductReleaseId; logs and uploaded diagnostics contain no credentials; and every shell interpolation crossing from workflow inputs is passed through a named environment variable and validated before use.","is_error_case":true}
FILE: /private/tmp/SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001.draft.json
TITLE: 
AC AC-001: {"id":"AC-001","criterion":"For a Callisto coordinated release, graph derivation emits exactly one ProductReleaseId with product `callisto`, one SemVer target shared by every releasable train member, and the exact tag `callisto@X.Y.Z`; divergent package target versions fail before an intent is written.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-002: {"id":"AC-002","criterion":"ReleaseOperationId no longer requires every operation to be owned by a package: registry publications remain keyed by exact ReleasePackageId, version, and RegistryBindingId; exactly one ProductTag follows all required registry publications; one ForgeDraft follows that tag; every ArtifactUpload follows the draft; and one ForgePublish follows every required asset. These operations address one ProductReleaseId and one GitHub Release object, and no per-package tag or forge-release operation can be derived for a coordinated train.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-003: {"id":"AC-003","criterion":"Workspace release selection excludes callisto-fixtures before the durable decision is constructed. It may receive the coordinated source version update, but it requires no changeset, creates no registry, tag, forge, artifact, or checksum operation, and can never block release completion. A test derives the real Callisto workspace decision and proves the exclusion rather than filtering a hand-built fixture after planning.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-004: {"id":"AC-004","criterion":"The product asset roster is a closed set of four payloads: a runnable `callisto` archive for aarch64-apple-darwin, a runnable statically linked `callisto` archive for x86_64-unknown-linux-musl, a runnable statically linked `callisto` archive for aarch64-unknown-linux-musl, and the callisto-moon plugin built for wasm32-wasip1. Any missing, duplicate, unexpected, differently targeted, or unsafe slot makes intent or manifest validation fail.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-005: {"id":"AC-005","criterion":"The macOS ARM64 payload is ad-hoc signed and verified locally, carries no Developer ID or notarization claim, and is documented as non-notarized; both Linux payloads are verified as the intended machine architecture and statically linked and pass a native `callisto --version` smoke test; the WASM payload is a release-profile wasm32-wasip1 build and passes the repository's real Moon/Extism sandbox smoke test.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-006: {"id":"AC-006","criterion":"The artifact manifest covers every registry upload artifact and every product payload with exact SHA-256 and byte length, is bound to the immutable intent digest and source commit, and rejects a byte change, slot substitution, source substitution, duplicate, omission, or extra entry before any release credential is exposed.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-007: {"id":"AC-007","criterion":"The GitHub Release asset roster contains the four payloads plus one deterministic `SHA256SUMS` file. SHA256SUMS lists each payload exactly once using its artifact-manifest digest; all five uploaded files have GitHub artifact attestations bound to the configured repository, immutable build workflow path and commit, and release source commit.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-008: {"id":"AC-008","criterion":"Every intent-declared artifact slot has exactly one production constructor, one build-manifest entry, and one reachable consumer operation; a compile-time exhaustive match or architecture test fails when a slot or operation variant is modeled but not derived, prepared, dispatched, observed, or covered by a boundary test.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-009: {"id":"AC-009","criterion":"The release pull request and user-facing notes present one product version and one GitHub Release while still listing the registry packages and their publication targets. The GitHub Release remains draft until every required payload, checksum, and attestation is observed exact, then becomes published once; generated documentation and CLI help contain no supported path that creates per-crate Callisto GitHub releases or treats callisto-fixtures as a release unit.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-010: {"id":"AC-010","criterion":"The revised durable types preserve the existing crate dependency direction: provider-neutral product, operation, and artifact identities live in callisto-model; release-unit resolution and intent derivation live in callisto-graph; callisto-cli and .github orchestration consume the intent and cannot independently invent the product tag, target roster, or artifact names.","is_error_case":false}
FILE: /private/tmp/SPEC-SETUP-IMMUTABLE-VERSION-005.draft.json
TITLE: 
AC AC-001: {"id":"AC-001","criterion":"An explicit X.Y.Z or callisto@X.Y.Z request resolves to that one semantic version and may install only a release asset or callisto-cli registry package with the identical version. Asset absence, registry absence, download error, extraction error, checksum mismatch, attestation mismatch, or installation failure exits nonzero and never invokes unpinned cargo install --git.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-002: {"id":"AC-002","criterion":"latest is resolved once to an immutable product version before installation and that resolved version is printed. Fallback between release assets and the registry retains that exact resolved version; it never asks each source independently for its latest version and never falls back to a branch.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-003: {"id":"AC-003","criterion":"source=local is the only mode that builds the current checkout, requires a Callisto workspace, rejects an exact release-version input, and reports the checkout commit and built CLI version. Merely running inside the Callisto monorepo cannot override source=auto, release, or registry.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-004: {"id":"AC-004","criterion":"Release-asset installation supports exactly aarch64-apple-darwin, x86_64-unknown-linux-musl, and aarch64-unknown-linux-musl. Unsupported operating systems and architectures fail with an actionable diagnostic rather than selecting a Linux or amd64 default.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-005: {"id":"AC-005","criterion":"Before extraction or PATH modification, a downloaded payload is matched to the exact product release, verified against that release's SHA256SUMS, and verified with GitHub artifact attestation for the configured Callisto repository and release build workflow. The installed binary must report the resolved version.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-006: {"id":"AC-006","criterion":"The resolver has table-driven action tests covering every source mode, both exact-version spellings, latest pinning, local-checkout precedence, each supported platform mapping, every unsupported-platform error, release-to-registry fallback with the same pinned version, and proof that no failure path executes an unpinned Git installation.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-007: {"id":"AC-007","criterion":"Source resolution, asset naming, version parsing, checksum verification, and attestation verification each have one canonical implementation used by every action path; sibling setup actions either call the same helper or explicitly document and test why their artifact type differs.","is_error_case":true}
FILE: /private/tmp/SPEC-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP-AUTHORITY-004.draft.json
TITLE: 
AC AC-001: {"id":"AC-001","criterion":"Cargo and uv use one shared typed TOML membership reader that returns Absent only when the manifest or relevant workspace table is genuinely absent, Present for a valid table including a deliberately empty members list, and a miette diagnostic error for read failure, TOML parse failure, malformed members/exclude fields, or invalid globs.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-002: {"id":"AC-002","criterion":"npm package.json and pnpm-workspace.yaml use the same Absent/Present/error semantics with format-specific parsers. If pnpm-workspace.yaml exists but is unreadable, invalid YAML, empty, lacks a valid packages sequence, contains a non-string item, or contains an invalid glob, discovery fails and never falls through to package.json or admit-all.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-003: {"id":"AC-003","criterion":"IgnoreWalkLocator::projects returns a discovery error when any selected root membership authority is invalid and cannot produce a partial project list. Workspace::load, every planning command, release decision derivation, and execution-time intent revalidation propagate that error before a decision, intent, manifest write, Git mutation, credential read, or provider invocation.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-004: {"id":"AC-004","criterion":"Absent authority retains the documented admit-all behavior only for the ecosystem whose authority is truly absent. Present empty membership denies non-root members, exclusions remain effective, hybrid roots retain their current valid behavior, and valid precedence between pnpm and package.json is unchanged.","is_error_case":false}
AC AC-005: {"id":"AC-005","criterion":"Diagnostics identify the ecosystem, safe workspace-relative authority path, invalid field or parser class, and remediation without exposing raw file contents. Distinct I/O, syntax, shape, and glob failures have stable diagnostic codes and sources.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-006: {"id":"AC-006","criterion":"Tests replace every current malformed-to-absent assertion with a failure assertion, cover each ecosystem's invalid syntax, wrong field shape, non-string item, and invalid glob, and include an end-to-end release-plan test proving malformed root authority cannot add an otherwise discoverable package to the release decision.","is_error_case":true}
AC AC-007: {"id":"AC-007","criterion":"All Cargo/uv membership call sites and all npm/pnpm membership call sites migrate in the same change; no second bool, Option, empty-glob, or best-effort parser remains able to encode invalid authority as absence or allow-all.","is_error_case":true}

